// digits_val's loop condition: whether the digit at `i` is in range must be
// re-evaluated every iteration, so it cannot be named once before the loop.
// n3.id already holds 3 functions and num/ has no room for a sibling file,
// so n3.id was promoted into this directory to make room.

more_digits(string s, int i, int radix) {
  int ok = 0;
  if(i < len(s)) {
    int c = charat(s, i);
    int d = dig_val(c);
    ok = d >= 0 && d < radix;
  }
} return int ok;
("42", 0, 10):(1)
("42", 2, 10):(0)
